## types_that_do_not_join
error[Z0214]: `fixture_fill` needs values of one type, but these are a Str and an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:19
  |
1 | fixture_fill("a", 1)
  |                   ^ an Int
  |
  = help: Int and Float join as Float, and NA fits any type; convert with `to` where a mixture is meant

## several_types_in_a_project_function
error[Z0101]: no type is called `Bool | Int`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:11
  |
2 | fn one(x: Bool | Int) -> Int {
  |           ^^^^^^^^^^ several types
  |
  = help: a parameter of several types belongs to a built-in's file (Engine and Project Specification, section 9.1); a project function declares one type, or takes a List

## join_in_a_project_function
error[Z0101]: no type is called `Join`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:20
  |
2 | fn same(x: Int) -> Join {
  |                    ^^^^ not a type
  |
  = help: the types of section 4: Bool, Int, Float, Str, Frame, Column<Float>, List<RegFit>, Var, Formula, Record, and the result types

## a_form_that_does_not_check
the Zeff source of core::bad_fixture does not build:
  error[Z0215]: `+` does not apply to text
   --> core/functions/bad_fixture.zeff:9:5
    |
  9 |     x + 1
    |     ^^^^^ text in arithmetic
    |
    = help: `join` puts texts together and `format` builds text from values (release 0.5.0); a number in text converts with `to(x, Float)` (with `x` read as a Str)

## too_many_forms
the Zeff source of core::bad_fixture does not build:
